WEBVTT

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.160
-He's getting away!
-Not for long!

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.360
(CHUCKLES)

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.720
GREM OVER RADIO:
He's dead, Professor.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.480
ZÜNDAPP: Wunderbar!

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.320
With Finn McMissile gone,
who can stop us now?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.560
Mater -Tow Mater, that's who -
is here to help you.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.720
(ENGINE CHOKING)

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.480
-Hey, Otis!
-Hey, Mater.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.000
I... Oh, gosh. I'm so sorry.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.360
I thought I could make it this time, but...

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.400
(ENGINE FAILS TO START)

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.800
Smooth like pudding, huh?

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.400
(SIGHS) Who am I kidding?
I'll always be a lemon.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.040
Well, dad-gum, you're leaking oil again.
Must be your gaskets.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.560
Hey, but look on the bright side.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.960
This is your tenth tow this month,
so it's on the house.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.480
You're the only one
that's nice to lemons like me, Mater.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.960
Don't sweat it. Shoot,
these things happen to everybody.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.400
-But you never leak oil.
-Yeah, but I ain't perfect.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.840
Don't tell nobody, but I think my rust
is starting to show through.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.760
Hey. Is Lightning McQueen back yet?

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.920
Not yet.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.600
He must be crazy excited
about winning his fourth Piston Cup.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.040
Four! Wow!

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.800
Yeah, we're so dad-gum proud of him,
but I wish he'd hurry up and get back,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.120
'cause we got a whole summer's worth
of best friend fun to make up for.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.440
Just me and... (GASPS)

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.600
(HORN HONKS)

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.080
McQueen!

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.440
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!
-McQueen!

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.120
-Mater! I'm in no hurry!
-Hey, everybody. McQueen's back!

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.080
-Aaah!
-McQueen's back!

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.120
-McQueen's back! McQueen's back!
-Aaah! Oooh-hoo! Oooh-hah!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.840
McQueen's back!

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.560
Oh, Lightning! Welcome home!

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.200
-Good to have you back, honey!
-Congratulations, man.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.560
Welcome home, soldier.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.000
The place wasn't the same without you,
son.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.720
What? Did he go somewhere?

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.280
-It's good to be home, everybody.
-(HORN HONKS)

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.760
-Mater!
-McQueen!

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.280
-Mater!
-McQueen!

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.960
Oooh!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.720
Whoooa!

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.760
Hey,
how far did you make it this time, Otis?

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.800
-Halfway to the county line.
-Ooh, not bad, man!

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.480
I know! I can't believe it either!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.440
-McQueen! Welcome back!
-Mater, it's so good to see you.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.800
You too, buddy.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.360
Oh, man, you ain't going to believe
the things I got planned for us!

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.560
These best friend greetings
get longer every year!

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.520
-You ready to have some serious fun?
-I've got something to show you first.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.680
MATER: Wow.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.200
I can't believe
they renamed the Piston Cup

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.400
after our very own Doc Hudson.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.880
I know Doc said these things
were just old cups,

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.200
but to have someone else win it
just didn't feel right, you know?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.200
Doc would've been real proud of you.
That's for sure.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.480
All right, pal.
I've been waiting all summer for this.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.720
-What you got planned?
-Ho-ho-ho! You sure you can handle it?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:45.280
Do you know who you're talking to?
This is Lightning McQueen!

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.360
I can handle anything.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.200
Er...Mater?

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.560
Just remember, your brakes
ain't going to work on these!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.560
-Mater?
-Relax.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.240
These train tracks
ain't been used in years!

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.400
-(TRAIN HORN)
-Aaaah!

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.560
-Aaaah!
-Faster, faster. Come on. Here we go!

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.120
Faster!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.200
(LAUGHS)

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.560
-(MATER CHUCKLES)
-Ooh. Wow.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.120
Yeah, I don't know. Do you think?

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.240
This is going to be good!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.320
(BLASTS HORN)

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.600
-(MATER LAUGHS)
-Did you see that?

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.760
(GURGLING)

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.840
MATER: Uh-oh.
This ain't going to be good.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.640
Ha-ha! Boy, this was the best day ever!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.120
And my favorite souvenir,
this new dent.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.760
-Boy, Mater, today was ah...
-Shoot, that was nothing.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.120
Wait till you see
what I got planned for tonight!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.560
Mater, Mater, whoa!
I was thinking of just a quiet dinner.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:53.000
That's exactly what I was thinkin'.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.440
-No, I meant with Sally, Mater.
-Even better!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.960
You, me and Miss Sally
goin' out for supper.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.280
Mater, I meant it would be
just me and Sally.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.600
-Oh.
-You know, just for tonight.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.640
-Oh...
-We'll do whatever you want tomorrow.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.680
OK.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.200
-Thanks for understanding.
-Yeah, sure.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.320
-Y'all go on and have fun now.
-All right, then.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.520
See you soon, amigo.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.640
(SIGHS)

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.600
SALLY: Ah, this is so nice.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:31.640
I can't tell you how good it is
to be here alone,

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.520
just the two of us, finally.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.080
-You and me.
-MATER: Ahem! Good evening.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.040
-Oh!
-My name is Mater,

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.680
and I'll be your waiter.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.400
Mater the waiter.
That's funny right there.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.480
Mater? You work here?

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.480
Yeah, I work here. What'd you think?

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.320
I snuck in here
when nobody was lookin'

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.040
and pretended to be your waiter
so I could hang out with you?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.920
Oh, yeah.
How ridiculous would that be?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.240
Can I start you two lovebirds off
with a couple of drinks?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.480
-Yes. I'll have my usual.
-You know what? I'll have that, too.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.440
Uh... Right. Your usual.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.520
(LAUGHTER)

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.560
(RATTLING)

